            <ArticleTitle>Transient left septal and anterior fascicular block associated with type 1 electrocardiographic Brugada pattern.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-0736(17)30210-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2017.07.015</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The left septal fascicular block (LSFB) or blockage of the middle fibers of the left bundle branch is probably caused mainly by - in the developed world - the proximal obstruction of the left anterior descending artery (LAD) before its first anterior septal perforator branch (S1). The association of transient LSFB and left anterior fascicular block (LAFB) - left bifascicular block - and the electrocardiographic type 1 Brugada pattern (BrP) has not been described in the literature yet.</AbstractText>
